---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Sumi Privacy Policy — Your Calculations Stay Yours"
  description="How Sumi stores calculations and preferences locally, handles optional tips and review prompts, and protects your privacy without ads or analytics."
>
  <section class="page-heading wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">YOUR CALCULATIONS STAY YOURS</p>
    <h1>
      Private.
      <br />
      <span>By design.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
      No ads. No analytics. No account.
      <br />
      Sumi does not upload your calculations.
    </p>
  </section>
  <article class="prose legal-prose wrap">
    <h2>Privacy policy</h2>
    <p class="policy-date">
      First published 27 August 2026. Updated{' '}
      <time datetime="2026-09-23">23 September 2026</time>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sumi is an independent scientific calculator made by Tomu Ozawa.
      Calculations work offline. The app has no account system, advertising,
      analytics or crash-reporting service, and does not send your calculations
      or local usage records to the developer.
    </p>
    <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Sumi saves calculation history, memory values, the expression being
      edited, calculation settings, and appearance and control preferences in
      the app’s local storage. It also saves support history and a small amount
      of information used to space out review requests, described below.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sumi does not operate a server that receives this information. Your
      operating system may include local app data in device backups or
      transfers, depending on your device and account settings. Those services
      are controlled by the platform provider.
    </p>
    <h2>Clearing your data</h2>
    <p>
      Open{' '}
      <strong>
        Settings → Calculation → Memory &amp; reset → Reset calculator
      </strong>{' '}
      to clear memory, calculation history and the current expression, and
      restore default calculation settings. This keeps appearance and control
      preferences, support history, and review request timing information.
    </p>
    <p>
      To remove all local Sumi data, use your device’s app storage controls or
      delete the app and its data. Device backups, store purchases and public
      reviews are managed separately through the relevant platform.
    </p>
    <h2>Tip jar purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Tips are optional one-time purchases and unlock no features. Google Play
      or the App Store handles payment through its billing service. The app
      receives purchase status and product and transaction identifiers, and
      stores a local tip count and transaction record so each purchase is
      counted once. It does not receive your payment card details, name or email
      address from the purchase.
    </p>
    <p>
      The store provides the developer with sales and financial reports. Store
      billing may connect to the internet to load prices, process a tip or
      finish a pending purchase. Apple’s and Google’s handling of store data is
      described in the{' '}
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple Privacy Policy</a>{' '}
      and the{' '}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Review requests</h2>
    <p>
      Sumi stores a limited calculation count, a few dates when calculations
      were completed, when review timing began, and dates of review request
      attempts or the <strong>Rate Sumi</strong> action. This information stays
      in local preferences and helps the app avoid asking for a review too early
      or too often. It is not sent to an analytics service or the developer.
    </p>
    <p>
      Review prompts use the platform’s own review service. The app is not told
      whether you submitted a review or what rating you chose. If you submit a
      store review, it is handled and may be published by Google or Apple under
      their policies. The developer can see public reviews and aggregate store
      reports.
    </p>
    <h2>Links, sharing and support email</h2>
    <p>
      Guides, support and privacy links open this website in your browser.{' '}
      <strong>Rate Sumi</strong> opens the store listing.{' '}
      <strong>Share Sumi</strong> opens your device’s share sheet with a
      download link; Sumi does not choose recipients or send a message
      automatically.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email the developer, your email address, message and any
      attachments you choose to send are received so your request can be
      answered. The in-app feedback action prepares an editable email with the
      app version and platform. You decide whether to send it.
    </p>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This website uses no visitor analytics, tracking cookies or advertising
      scripts. Fonts and images are served with the site. The example controls
      work in your browser and do not send your selections anywhere.
    </p>
    <p>
      Google Play links contain campaign labels identifying this website and the
      referring page. These labels contain no personal identifier. Google
      processes visits and downloads under its own policies. Google Search
      Console and store reports can provide aggregate information about search
      discovery and download interest.
    </p>
    <p>
      The website is hosted on GitHub Pages. Hosting services process
      information needed to deliver pages, such as IP addresses. See the{' '}
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
        GitHub Privacy Statement
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Sumi is suitable for a general audience. The app does not ask for age or
      other personal details, and the developer does not knowingly collect
      personal information from children. If a child has sent personal
      information by email, contact the developer to request its deletion.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If Sumi’s behaviour changes in a way that affects your privacy, this page
      will be updated and the revision date above changed.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy can be sent to{' '}
      <a href="mailto:hello@sumicalculator.com">hello@sumicalculator.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
